1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,308
Can a phone flag a defect and
tell an operator what to do?

2
00:00:03,418 --> 00:00:05,284
Here’s SurfaceNet, working offline.

3
00:00:05,753 --> 00:00:08,992
On a production line, a scratch
and a reflection can look alike.

4
00:00:09,102 --> 00:00:11,078
Miss the scratch and a bad part can ship.

5
00:00:11,188 --> 00:00:14,254
Hold the good part and an
operator has to inspect it again.

6
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:18,560
SurfaceNet turns a mounted phone
into an offline inspection station.

7
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:22,489
Open Rear camera and enroll a
verified clean part as a reference.

8
00:00:22,599 --> 00:00:25,661
If the image lacks detail, the
app asks for a new capture.

9
00:00:26,153 --> 00:00:29,524
Here’s an annotated production
specimen from our held-out test set.

10
00:00:29,634 --> 00:00:33,730
SurfaceNet outlines the mark and estimates
severity from its shape and size.

11
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:37,986
For a held part, the operator can check
the same mark under a second light.

12
00:00:38,096 --> 00:00:42,553
The app aligns the two captures and checks
whether the same defect pixels persist.

13
00:00:42,663 --> 00:00:47,548
This replay simulates the second exposure.
An inconclusive check keeps the part on hold.

14
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:53,631
Tap Ask local Llama. Llama 3.2 runs
on the Arm CPU through ExecuTorch.

15
00:00:53,741 --> 00:00:59,010
Here it recommends keeping the part segregated and
asking quality engineering to verify pit depth.

16
00:00:59,487 --> 00:01:01,782
Enter a part ID and save the inspection.

17
00:01:01,892 --> 00:01:06,756
Trace log reopens the mask, decision
and advice. Export the record as CSV.

18
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:11,333
Under Device, compare the vision
profiles and export live camera timings.

19
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:19,431
On 1,004 held-out images, four-view
INT8 reached 97.45% image AUROC.

20
00:01:19,541 --> 00:01:24,591
Both profiles sent 105 of 110
defects to alert or review.

21
00:01:24,701 --> 00:01:31,483
Four views reduced clean referrals
from 165 to 130. That’s 21% fewer.

22
00:01:31,953 --> 00:01:36,216
From the first inspection to a saved
decision, the whole workflow runs offline.
